n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        fmt: str,\n        datefmt: str | None = None,\n        high_precision: bool = False,\n        use_color: bool = False,\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n```\nnew: adds keyword-only param and validation.\n\nEdit 2 logger: replace format body:\n```\n    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        msg = super().format(record)\n```\nnew:\n```\n    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        max_chars = self.max_message_chars\n        if max_chars is None or getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is True:\n            return self._format(record)\n        saved_msg, saved_args = record.msg, record.args\n        try:\n            message = record.getMessage()\n            if len(message) > max_chars:\n                record.msg = _truncate_message(message, max_chars)\n                record.args = None\n            return self._format(record)\n        finally:\n            record.msg = saved_msg\n            record.args = saved_args\n\n    def _format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        msg = super().format(record)\n```\n\nAnd a module-level helper _truncate_message + marker constant. Place after _COLOR_RESET:\n\n```\n_OMITTED_MARKER = \"...<omitted>...\"\n\n\ndef _truncate_message(message: str, max_chars: int) -> str:\n    remaining = max_chars - len(_OMITTED_MARKER)\n    head = (remaining + 1) // 2\n    tail = remaining - head\n    return f\"{message[:head]}{_OMITTED_MARKER}{message[len(message) - tail:] if tail else ''}\"\n```\n\nCareful tail=0 → message[-0:] is whole string; guard. remaining >= 32-15=17 >0 so tail≥8. Still guard fine.\n\nEdit 3 logger _setup_logger: add max_message_chars=... and import envs.\n\nActually import: add `from deepinfer.environ import envs` in imports. Where? After `from types import TracebackType`. Replace:\n\n```\nfrom types import Tracebac